        "text": "Michael Scott’s serious girlfriends mentioned in the context are:\n\n1. Jan Levinson  \n- Michael considered Jan to be his girlfriend and they had a sexual relationship. However, Jan did not consider Michael to be her boyfriend. Michael said, \"Yes, I had sex with Jan, and yes, I did consider Jan to be my girlfriend. However, Jan clearly didn't consider me to be her boyfriend.\"  \n- The relationship ended ambiguously; Jan gave Michael poor performance reviews even after their relationship became official, indicating a troubled relationship. The exact ending is not detailed in the context. (S07E04)\n\n2. Tara  \n- Michael refers to Tara as his girlfriend who lives in New York City and gave him a toy taxi cab as a gift. He says, \"My girlfriend Tara, who lives in New York City.\"  \n- No information about how the relationship ended is provided in the context. (S07E04)\n\n3. Carol  \n- Michael was engaged to Carol, having proposed on their fourth date. Carol says, \"You proposed to me on our fourth date.\"  \n- The relationship ended after Michael found out he had herpes, which he told Carol about. Carol expressed that Michael made a bigger deal out of things than necessary, and Michael reflects that their engagement \"just seems ridiculous\" now. (S07E04)\n\n4. European girlfriend  \n- Michael mentions having a European girlfriend who is a dental hygienist from Carbondale. He says, \"I already have my European girlfriend.\"  \n- No information about how the relationship ended is provided in the context. (S07E04)\n\nNo other serious girlfriends are supported by the context. The endings are only explicitly mentioned for Carol (ended after herpes revelation) and Jan (relationship troubled, no clear ending given). For Tara and the European girlfriend, the context does not provide how the relationships ended.",
